Article 12
(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to implement efforts to protect victims of violence in the form of:
 a. preventing the occurrence of all forms of gender-based and child violence;
 b. providing protection by providing complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal aid and enforcement services, repatriation and social reintegration services, seeking to increase community participation, as well as monitoring and reporting;
 c. encouraging and increasing community participation;
 d. cooperating with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and recover victims of violence.
(2) To carry out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to:
 a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based and child violence;
 b. establish an integrated service center;
 c. establish complaint service institutions at the sub-district level;
 d. facilitate the implementation of integrated service centers and activities of complaint service institutions at the sub-district level;
 e. provide facilities and infrastructure;
 f. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
 g. conduct coordination and cooperation in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based and child violence;
 h. encourage and increase community participation;
 i. conduct monitoring and evaluation.
(3) In the implementation of its obligations, responsibilities and authorities, the Regent may delegate to the relevant SKPD.
(4) The relevant SKPD receiving delegation from the Regent as referred to in paragraph (3) shall in its implementation prepare a Regional Action Plan for the protection of victims.

CHAPTER VIII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 36
(1) The community may participate in assisting efforts to prevent and handle victims of gender-based violence against women and children.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
 a. providing information and/or reporting any violence that comes to their knowledge;
 b. providing protection for victims;
 c. providing emergency assistance;
 d. providing advocacy to victims and/or the community regarding the handling of gender-based violence against women and children;
 e. assisting in the process of submitting applications for the determination of protection;
 f. assisting in the process of returning and social reintegration.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.

Article 24
Increasing community participation as referred to in Article 16, letter h is carried out by means of:
a. fostering community awareness of cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
b. encouraging the community to actively participate in providing information and reporting the occurrence of gender-based violence and violence against children;
c. fostering local wisdom in handling gender-based violence and violence against children;
d. organizing the strengthening of community groups in handling gender-based violence and violence against children;
e. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to gender-based violence and violence against children.

Article 29
LPPTK as referred to in Article 28, has the duties of: a. receiving complaints of cases of gender-based violence and violence against children; b. providing initial consultation to victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;
c. conducting crisis intervention for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;
d. providing referrals for handling cases of gender-based violence and violence against children to PPT PKBGA.

Article 23
Coordination and cooperation as referred to in Article 16, letter g includes:
a. conducting coordination and cooperation in handling cases of violence with complaint service institutions at the sub-district level;
b. conducting coordination and cooperation with integrated service centers between regencies/cities;
c. conducting coordination and cooperation with institutions providing services for victims of gender-based violence and children;
d. conducting coordination and consultation with the Regional Government.

Article 32
(1) Every victim of gender-based violence and every child victim has the right to: a. obtain protection for personal, family and property security, and freedom from threats related to testimony that will be, is being, or has been given; b. participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;
c. freedom from ensnaring questions;
d. obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions;
e. obtain complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal aid and enforcement services, as well as repatriation and social reintegration services.
(2) The rights of victims as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES, OBJECTIVES AND SCOPE
Article 2
The Principles of Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children are:
a. non-discrimination;
b. best interests of victims;
c. gender justice and equality;
d. victim protection;
e. maternal survival;
f. survival, growth, and development of children;
g. respect for the views of children;
h. transparency;
i. integration;
j. not blaming victims;
k. empowerment;
l. victim confidentiality;
m. decision-making in the hands of victims.

REGENT OF BANYUMAS
CENTRAL JAVA PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANYUMAS REGENCY
NUMBER 3 OF 2015
CONCERNING
THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION
FOR VICTIMS OF GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE AND CHILD VICTIMS
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF BANYUMAS,

Considering : a. that all forms of acts of violence, especially gender-based violence and violence against children constitute violations of human rights and crimes against human dignity;
b. that victims of gender-based violence and violence against children in the Region continue to increase;
c. that victims of violence need to have their dignity protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination;
d. that based on Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, and letter d, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Child Victims;

In View of 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 13 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within Central Java Province;
3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);
5. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);
6. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
7. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning the Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
8. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
9. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);
10. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended by Government Regulation in Lieu of a Law Number 2 of 2014 concerning Amendments to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 246, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5589);
11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
12. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);
13. Regional Regulation of Central Java Province Number 03 of 2009 concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Child Victims (Regional Gazette of Central Java Province of 2009 Number 3, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Central Java Province Number 20);

With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BANYUMAS REGENCY, and

